  // RigScope peripheral catalogue. Read by src/RigScope.Core/Peripherals/PeripheralCatalogue.cs.
  // - suites: ids must match KnownAppsProbe.Catalogue so RigScope knows whether they run and start with Windows.
  //   noDevice = what it means when no device of that vendor is connected: "notNeeded" only for suites that drive
  //   nothing but peripherals; "unknown" when the suite may also control RAM, fans or the motherboard.
  //   features[].inUseWhen is a regex on Windows device names (Device Manager), e.g. Sonar's virtual audio devices.
  // - vendors: USB vendor ids → suite. requireName is for ids shared with other products (HP, Atmel).
  //   Device families match by name regex first, product id second.
  //   onboardMemory: yes / no / unknown. Only write "yes" or "no" when an official page says so; otherwise "unknown".
  //   Unknown models from a known vendor get the vendor's fallback, which must say "check", not guess.
  //   Product ids under "pids" were seen in a real Windows device list; they are a second way to match, not a spec.
  // - Vendor ids: http://www.linux-usb.org/usb.ids (2026-06-26) unless a vendor lists its own source.
